message: "If you use Revelado or its technical documentation, please cite it as below."
title: "Revelado: develop your RAW photos like a film lab"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Peña Sanchez"
    given-names: "Jorge Luis"
    alias: "bluestudiobrooks-gif"
  - name: "Claude (Anthropic)"
    alias: "AI co-creator"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Blue-Studio-Lab/Revelado"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: "0.2.0-beta.1"
date-released: "2026-11-17"
keywords:
  - raw-photo
  - photography
  - film-emulation
  - denoising
  - chromatic-aberration
  - photo-culling
abstract: >-
  Open-source RAW developer that runs on your own computer. It provides
  physically based colour-negative film emulation (density curves, interlayer
  effects, grain in density space, scanner model), RAW-domain noise and
  chromatic-aberration cleanup dosed by ISO and exposure push, technical photo
  culling, and optional AI assistance.
